  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Integrity for Recovery in Yemen</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Corruption is a structural deep-rooted challenge in Yemen, accentuated by the intricate nexus between corruption and conflict. Costs go well beyond financial loss and are visible in the dismal state of human development, and the opportunities lost for a better future. Yemen had ratified the UNCAC in 2005 and made key steps to implement it; however, these efforts have hit a standstill since 2014. The opportunity to restart them is now revived thanks to the recent steps</narrative>
  </description>
